course: dictionary
lesson: 15363
title: A word from French
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come into English from other languages. Sou is a French word, and you will mostly meet it in old stories and history lessons. A sou was an old French coin worth very little. «The beggar held out his hand, but he did not have a single sou.» The clue is that he is begging for help, so a sou must be a small amount of money.
explain: The phrase «not a sou» is old-fashioned. It means having no money at all. «He had spent his wages and hadn't a sou left for the bus.» The sentence tells you he is broke, so the meaning fits: no money.
explain: Be careful, because sous (said soo) is a different word. In French it means under, and in a kitchen a sous-chef is the second chef, the one under the head chef. «The sous-chef chopped the onions while the head chef cooked the fish.» Use the context to decide which meaning you need.
fact: A sou was an old French coin of very little value.
fact: «Not a sou» means having no money at all, as in «he hasn't a sou».
fact: «Sous» means under in French, as in sous-chef.
fact: A sous-chef is the second chef in a kitchen, working under the head chef.
fact: Sou and sous are both said like the English word sue, so the context tells you which one is meant.
exercise: «The poor family did not have a sou to buy bread.» What does not have a sou mean? | They had a lot of gold coins | *They had no money at all | They had a little money | They were late for the shop
exercise: «In the kitchen, the sous-chef peeled the potatoes.» What is a sous-chef? | A waiter who takes orders | The head chef who runs the kitchen | *The second chef, working under the head chef | A cook who only bakes cakes
exercise: In French, «sous» means what? | Very old | Above | Money | *Under
test: «The old coin was a sou, worth very little.» What was a sou? | A kind of bus ticket | *An old French coin of very little value | A type of bread | A large gold coin
test: «Ella hasn't a sou, so she cannot buy a drink.» What does hasn't a sou mean? | *She has no money at all | She has forgotten her purse | She has one big coin | She has a lot of money
exam: In the sentence «The sous-chef stirs the soup for the head chef», what does sous-chef mean? | A bowl for soup | A cook who only makes desserts | *The second chef, who works under the head chef | The head chef
